{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1078246-leviathan-the-cult","id":1078246,"title":"Leviathan: the Cult","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-14T03:01:21-07:00","id":1078246,"title":"Leviathan: the Cult","content":"I know nothing about this game. What does it offer that is not already subsumed into the Makara splat in Beast? Just wondering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our society is held together by the thinnest of threads: that exquisitely refined sense of tribal order.<br /> Edith Wharton, The Age of Innocence<br /> <br /> I am a huge fan of both the Trinity Universe and the classic World of Darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12799-spellfire22","name":"Spellfire22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:54:19-07:00","id":1078744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spellfire22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1078246-leviathan-the-cult#post1078246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know nothing about this game. What does it offer that is not already subsumed into the Makara splat in Beast? Just wondering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters, it approaches family in exactly the opposite direction to Beast.<br /> <br /> Beast takes the view of family as a group of people with whom you voluntarily bond and associate. &quot;You choose your family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Leviathan goes the exact opposite direction, a family of blood with no choice in the matter, regardless of how shitty they are. &quot;You <i>don't</i> choose your family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that it is objectively <i>not fun</i> to be a Leviathan, and a Leviathan who tries to use their supernatural state as a force for good is basically about as likely to succeed as a man looking for ice water in Hell. Beasts might be able to do some good, if they're so inclined, and can at least remain relatively harmless if they try. A Leviathan's mere <i>presence</i> hollows out the souls of those nearby, and turns anywhere you remain into Innsmouth 2.0.<br /> <br /> There's an aesthetic similarity with the Makara, and Leviathan/Beast interactions are very fertile ground for all sorts of neat stories, but the two are really not the same. I encourage you to go read up on Leviathan, and maybe take a look at the Leviathan 2E project. It's got some real neat stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}